# Database Rules - Greek ERP/CRM System

## Core Technology Standards

- **Primary Database**: PostgreSQL 16+ for ACID compliance and JSON support
- **Cache Database**: Redis 7.2+ for sessions, caching, and job queues
- **Local Database**: SQLite with encryption for desktop deployments
- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy with declarative models and Alembic migrations
- **Connection Pooling**: AsyncPG with connection pooling for performance

## Database Architecture (MANDATORY)

- **Separate Database per Company**: Each company gets dedicated database (erp*company*{id})
- **Smart Resource Pooling**: Small companies share PostgreSQL instances, large companies get dedicated
- **Partitioning Strategy**: Yearly partitions for business entities, monthly for high-volume transactions
- **Multi-Schema**: Use schemas within each company DB (core, crm, erp, config, audit, custom)
- **No Shared Tables**: Zero write contention, complete performance isolation

## Table Design Standards

- **Primary Keys**: Always use UUID, never auto-increment integers
- **Audit Fields**: created_at, updated_at, created_by on ALL tables
- **Soft Deletes**: Use is_deleted flag, never hard delete business data
- **Custom Fields**: JSONB column for EspoCRM-style extensibility
- **Partitioning**: Implement on high-volume tables (invoices, orders, transactions)

## Partitioning Strategy (MANDATORY)

- **Business Entity Tables**: Yearly partitions by created_at
- **Transaction Tables**: Monthly partitions by transaction_date
- **Historical Access**: All data always available, no fiscal year switching
- **Automatic Pruning**: PostgreSQL handles partition selection automatically
- **Archive Strategy**: Hot (current+2 years), Warm (3-7 years), Cold (7+ years)

## Greek Compliance Requirements (When Applicable)

- **AFM Storage**: Encrypted Greek tax numbers with validation
- **DOY Reference**: Greek tax office lookup tables in each company DB
- **VAT Rates**: Location-aware Greek VAT rate configuration per company
- **AADE Integration**: Company-specific tracking tables for MyDATA submissions
- **Historical Reporting**: Multi-year tax reports via partition unions

## Database Operations Automation

- **Company Provisioning**: Automated database creation with full schema
- **Migration Management**: Automated migrations across all company databases
- **Resource Scaling**: Dynamic scaling from shared to dedicated instances
- **Backup Orchestration**: Company-specific backup schedules and retention
- **Monitoring**: Per-company database performance monitoring

## Performance Requirements

- **Write Isolation**: Zero cross-company write contention
- **Partition Pruning**: <50ms for partitioned queries, <500ms for complex joins
- **Connection Pooling**: Company-specific connection pools
- **Resource Allocation**: CPU/memory based on company size and usage patterns
- **Auto-scaling**: Automatic migration between shared/dedicated instances

## Backup & Recovery Strategy

- **Multi-Level Backups**: Continuous WAL, daily full, weekly cross-region, monthly archive
- **Company-Specific**: Individual backup and restore per company
- **Point-in-Time Recovery**: WAL-based recovery for any timestamp
- **Greek Compliance**: 5+ year retention for legal requirements
- **Encrypted Storage**: All backups encrypted with company-specific keys

## Security Standards

- **Database Isolation**: Complete separation between companies
- **Encryption**: Sensitive data (AFM, personal info) encrypted at rest
- **Access Control**: Company-specific database credentials
- **Network Security**: VPC isolation for company database clusters
- **Audit Logging**: All database operations logged per company

## Data Seeding Requirements

- **Greek Reference Data**: Tax offices (DOY), VAT rates, postal codes per company
- **Test Data**: Realistic Greek business scenarios for development
- **Production Seeds**: Essential configuration and lookup data
- **Automated Seeding**: New company databases automatically seeded

## Migration Standards

- **Company-Parallel Execution**: Run migrations across all company DBs in parallel
- **Rollback Strategy**: Per-company rollback capability
- **Testing**: Test migrations on copy of production company data
- **Automated Verification**: Verify migration success across all companies

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never create shared tables between companies
- ❌ Don't skip partitioning on high-volume tables
- ❌ Never hardcode company database connections
- ❌ Don't create foreign keys across company boundaries
- ❌ Never skip automated backup verification
- ❌ Don't store sensitive data unencrypted
- ❌ Never create migrations without parallel execution strategy
- ❌ Don't skip Greek compliance validation in database
- ❌ Never use SELECT \* on partitioned tables without WHERE clause
- ❌ Don't forget to implement partition pruning strategies

- ❌ Never use SELECT \* in production code
- ❌ Don't forget to partition large audit tables
